// Fills a database with a fictional household's finances: six full months of history plus the
// current month, dated relative to "today" so it never looks stale. Used by
// `npm run seed:demo` (sample data to look around with) and by the public demo's periodic
// reset.
//
// Importable from a plain tsx script AND from inside Next, so: no `server-only`, no
// `@/server/db`, no `next/*`. It takes the connection it should write to.
//
// The data is generated by simulating the household day by day — paychecks, bills, card
// payments, transfers, card swipes — while tracking every account's balance, so the balance
// snapshots, the transactions and the bill sheets all tell the same story. Everything is
// deterministic for a given day (seeded PRNG), and every name and number is made up.

